11
01:04:25,714 --> 01:04:31,714
Fish Tank is a 2009 British coming of age drama film
written and directed by Andrea Arnold.

12
01:10:17,142 --> 01:10:23,142
The film is about Mia, a volatile and socially isolated 15-year-old,
and her relationship with her mother's new boyfriend.

13
01:16:08,571 --> 01:16:14,571
Fish Tank was critically acclaimed and won the Jury
Prize at the 2009 Cannes Film Festival.

14
01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:06,000
It also won the 2010 BAFTA for Best British Film.

15
01:27:51,428 --> 01:27:57,428
It was ranked 65th on the BBC's 100 Greatest Films of the 21st Century list.

16
01:33:42,857 --> 01:33:48,857
It was also ranked 91st on The New York Times' list of
the 100 Best Movies of the 21st Century.

17
01:39:34,285 --> 01:39:40,285
The film was funded by BBC Films and the UK Film Council.

18
01:45:25,714 --> 01:45:31,714
It was theatrically released in the United Kingdom
on 11 September 2009 by Curzon Film.

19
01:51:17,142 --> 01:51:23,142
The film explores themes of adultery, friendship, mother, alcohol, fight.

20
01:57:08,571 --> 01:57:14,571
The tone is emotional.
